 "F_what_holds": "(1) union-find + component-level family count does let 1,148 one-family and 868 no-strong nodes inherit conviction — verified; (2) ~814 of the 1,566 (52%, 1.34% of points) look human by nonce/ENS and 10/12 sampled from those strata are aged active wallets — a real precision gain; (3) per-sample gating is standard prior art.",
 "G_what_fails": "(1) 'affected_wallets_estimate 1,566' as honest wallets is overstated by ~40%: >=301 farm-like by cache signature (237 Bitget-6-funded), +180 fresh, +271 indeterminate incl. sleepers; (2) the recall claim omits a 100% loss on a confirmed 232-wallet farm and 78% loss on flagged ring99; (3) the STRONG/WEAK split treats shared_hub as weak even when every hub-funded member is nonce-0 with deposit+0.0098 funding and an immediate sweep — the suggested fix as written is not deployable; (4) 365/367 = 99.46%, not >=99.5%.",
 "H_strongest_supported_version": "Per-node family counting is a legitimate precision control that would free ~800-1,000 human-looking wallets (~1.3-2.5% of points), but only if paired with a rule that keeps fresh, hub-funded, swept single-deposit wallets (e.g. hub edges count as strong when both endpoints are nonce 0 / funded deposit+dust) — otherwise it hands back the entire Bitget-6 operator (238 of 241 wallets) and most of ring99.",
